<title>USA: Typhoon moves over sea after crossing Honshu - WSC.</title>
<headline>Typhoon moves over sea after crossing Honshu - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical storm Opal has moved back off the east coast of Honshu, Japan, and is moving rapidly out to sea after having crossed Honshu during the past 24 hours, private forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Friday.</p>
<p>Conditions will improve during the next six hours as the system moves away from the area.</p>
